# Reuse Shared UI

## Core rule
- Before creating a new composable or UI model, **search** for an existing one with the same visual/data shape.
- If a match exists: **reuse it**, or rename/generalize it into `ui/components/` (or a shared section host). Do **not** rewrite a parallel copy per screen or per row.
- Repeated blocks on one page (e.g. five Top rated / New in rows) = **one** row composable + a list of section models — not five near-duplicate files.
- Screen-specific wrappers only when props or layout truly diverge.
- Shared chrome (header + chevron + `LazyRow` + desktop arrows) stays **one** implementation parameterized by content.

## Do
- Prefer extending or renaming an existing card/row when the next screen needs the same pattern.
- Pass different mock/title data into the shared composable instead of forking the UI.

## Do not
- Copy-paste a section file and tweak strings for each category row.
- Invent a second product/merchant card that duplicates an existing one with only a new name.

## When to use
- Always, for any new or refined UI component/section in this repo.

## When to update
- New shared component naming conventions settle.
- A pattern is generalized out of a screen-specific package into `ui/components/`.
